{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3000","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3000","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3000\",\"parent_revision\":\"13850f0fa90a5f9bd851110bea82b381af0e370bb6af6608817a174446ad6fb2\",\"root_revision\":\"13850f0fa90a5f9bd851110bea82b381af0e370bb6af6608817a174446ad6fb2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`/dh:work-backlog-item` (and `/dh:create-backlog-item`, which redirects to it) failed reproducibly in an agent session on 2026-08-19, at skill-load time, on every invocation attempted \u2014 including a content-free `--help` and a bare retry seconds later:\\n\\n```\\nShell command failed for pattern \\\"!`...`\\\": [stderr]\\n(eval):1: permission denied: ../..\\n```\\n\\nThe failing line is the `<gate_token>` bang-exec in `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` (line 9):\\n\\n```\\n!`node \\\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/get-gate-token.mjs\\\"`\\n```\\n\\n**Falsification check performed:** running the exact target script directly via the Bash tool with an absolute path (`node \\\"/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/scripts/get-gate-token.mjs\\\"`) succeeded immediately and produced a valid-looking token (`<uuid>:<64-hex>`), confirming the script itself is not the fault \u2014 the failure is specific to how Claude Code's `!`...`` bang-exec substitution resolves and executes this particular line at skill-load time in this session.\\n\\n**Comparison control:** `/dh:dh-meta-docs`, a different skill in the same plugin using a `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}`-based bang-exec (`find ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs -name '*.md' -type f | sort`), loaded and substituted correctly in the same session \u2014 ruling out a session-wide bang-exec outage. The failure appears isolated to `work-backlog-item`'s specific gate-token line, its `shell: bash` frontmatter field (present on this skill; not confirmed present/absent on the control skill), and/or `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}` substitution specifically (as opposed to `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}`) \u2014 not yet isolated further.\\n\\n**Session context:** the failing session's cwd was a git worktree (`/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/.claude/worktrees/section-roundtrip-tests`), not the primary checkout \u2014 worth checking as a variable, though not yet confirmed as causal (no comparison run from the primary checkout was performed in the same session).\\n\\n**Impact \u2014 this is P0, not P1/P2:** `/dh:work-backlog-item create` is the mandated entry point for capturing backlog items per this repo's own `.claude/CLAUDE.md` Session Start item 4 (\\\"Multi-step work identified: capture new backlog items via `/dh:work-backlog-item create -- ...`\\\") and `AGENTS.md`'s Request Progression section. `backlog_add`'s MCP tool schema hard-requires a `gate_token` sourced from this exact bang-exec line and explicitly rejects direct calls and manually-reproduced tokens (confirmed: regenerating the token by running the script directly and passing it to `backlog_add` was rejected server-side with `\\\"Direct backlog_add calls are not permitted. Load and follow /dh:work-backlog-item create...\\\"` \u2014 meaning the gate validates more than token-file presence, and no further bypass is safe or possible). With this bang-exec broken, there is **no working path** to create a structured backlog item in an affected session \u2014 the only fallback is a raw `gh issue create` bypassing all grooming, dedup, and templating.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Root cause of the `permission denied: ../..` failure isolated (candidates to check first: the skill's `shell: bash` frontmatter field's interaction with bang-exec resolution; `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}` substitution specifically vs. `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}`; worktree cwd vs. primary checkout cwd)\\n- [ ] Fix applied and the fix is falsification-tested: `/dh:work-backlog-item create -- \\\"<test>\\\"` succeeds end-to-end from a worktree session with `shell: bash` frontmatter intact\\n- [ ] A regression check exists that would have caught this (per this repo's \\\"Close criteria\\\" convention) \u2014 e.g. a smoke-test invocation of the skill, or a script-level test asserting the bang-exec line's exact substituted form is a valid, executable shell command\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer or agent relying on the backlog-capture pipeline**, I want to **create backlog items through `/dh:work-backlog-item create`** so that **I don't need to bypass the structured grooming/dedup/gate-token workflow with a raw `gh issue create`**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered while attempting to file issue #2999 via `/dh:work-backlog-item create` in an agent session on 2026-08-19; the structured route was blocked, so #2999 was filed via `gh issue create` directly as a documented fallback.\\n- **Priority**: P0 \u2014 every consumer of the mandated backlog-capture entry point is blocked in an affected session, with no legitimate workaround (the gate correctly rejects direct `backlog_add` calls).\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Related**: #2999 (the substantive item this investigation was trying to file when the blocker was hit)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e4ee814030775bc0c5ac05ad7202cf5be516c49e06631875a0c8982b8288821f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiJ8RQ\"}"}